Oracle staging qualification update
Base for this patch is codex/staging-infra at a0e6cecd81c5a583c89510edbfec5cea9dc8cc89.
Apply this patch from the root of that infrastructure checkout.

The browser image supplies the exact revision's executable, static files,
Rust sources for feature-flag discovery, and contract fixtures for outbox
tests. Python generates the pinned negative catalogue candidate and OpenSSL
generates ephemeral test certificates.

The Compose changes give browser qualification a temporary PostgreSQL 18.6
cluster. Browser and PostgreSQL share loopback on a separate internal network.
The namespace allows the CI launcher's SMTP ports 465 and 587. PostgreSQL
data uses a fresh anonymous volume. Keys and reports use bounded tmpfs.

A default deployment builds only the runtime. An explicit browser request
prepares the fixture stack and runs the selected spec or the full project.

The deployment script generates independent credentials for that cluster,
starts it before the browser and removes it after completion or timeout.
The browser calls local.mjs and run.mjs with the launcher's private environment
file. The launcher supplies Game and payment fixtures, enabled test flags,
OAuth configuration, sources, seed data and legal pages. The isolated
database also gets the existing offline password-range fixture so credential
changes and recovery can exercise the normal verifier. Oracle retains
deployed-stack readiness and keeps its tunnel-facing flags and data
independent of qualification.

Periodic sandbox admin reads keep the shared staff fixture active during
long runs under the normal session lifetime rules.
The browser also gets a private executable tmpfs for the generated launcher
used by the character creation harness.

The runner keeps the existing literal spec filter and a two-hour CI browser
budget. It reports pass, fail and skip counts and test identities. It leaves
raw assertion messages and browser artifacts inside the temporary container.
The infrastructure tests check loopback isolation, credential separation,
full spec collection, the time budget and cleanup.

